# What a rule is

A rule looks at what a call IS and picks a policy -- an ordered chain of
places to look for a model. It does not name a model and it does not
name a chain. Rules are tried in precedence order and the first match
wins.

# The condition vocabulary

These are the only keys a condition may use on this cluster. A key
outside this list produces a rule that refuses to load, and the person
is left believing a rule is protecting them.

{{ range .whenKeys }}  {{ . }}
{{ end }}
  level        what the call declares it needs
  modality     chat, streamingChat, tools, streamingTools, structured,
               embedding, vision, transcribe, speech
  prompt       the DSL prompt name the call renders
  role         the AGENT's role slug
  actorRole    the calling human's cluster role -- a different question
               from role: an operator watching a non-operator agent is
               not an operator turn
  tag          a call tag, such as background
  touches      the call's footprint: concept ids, matched by prefix.
               This is the key for "anything that touches X"

