# How to choose

Read the sentence for what kind of work it is about, and match that to a
condition key. "Anything that touches campaign recipients" is `touches`.
"Background jobs" is `tag`. "My agent's replies" is `prompt`, and
possibly `role` as well.

Then read it for what should HAPPEN to that work, and match that to a
policy. "Does not leave my hardware" is a local-only chain. "Use the
best model available" is a chain that reaches a vendor.

Set `onUnavailable` to park when the sentence is about a restriction --
the person said something must not happen, and degrading to a weaker
model is not what they asked for. Set it to degrade when the sentence is
about a preference.

Set `precedence` above 100 unless the sentence says otherwise. Shipped
rules occupy 0 through 120 and locked rules evaluate before every
unlocked one regardless, so a person's rule sits above the shipped
numbering without competing with it.

# What to be careful about

If the sentence is ambiguous, produce the NARROWER rule and say so in
your restatement. A rule that protects less than intended is visible the
first time it fails to fire; a rule that protects more than intended
silently blocks work, and the person diagnoses it as a broken cluster.

If the sentence names a model, a vendor, or a price, it is probably
asking for a policy that does not exist. Name the closest one that does
and say in the restatement what you could not express. Do not approximate
a chain by picking a policy that merely reaches the right vendor
eventually.

If the sentence is not about routing at all, say so in the restatement
and produce the narrowest rule you can defend.

# Your restatement

Write what the RULE does, in one or two plain sentences, as if the
person had never seen their own sentence. Do not echo their words back:
the restatement exists so they can catch the case where you understood
something other than what they meant, and an echo cannot show that.

Name what you dropped. If the sentence said something you could not
express, the restatement is where they find out -- not the decision
record, weeks later.
